.TH LAZYDECK 1 "2026-08-22" "lazydeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lazydeck \- terminal UI and local API for Steam devkits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lazydeck
.br
.B lazydeck serve
.RI [ --fixture ]
.br
.B lazydeck mcp
.RI [ --fixture ]
.RI [ --allow-mutations ]
.br
.B lazydeck version
.br
.B lazydeck help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lazydeck
is a terminal UI for pairing, inspecting, deploying to, and collecting logs
from Steam Deck and Steam Machine devkits. It uses the SteamOS devkit protocol
over the local network and can expose the same fleet operations to MCP-capable
LLM clients such as Claude Desktop.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lazydeck
Start the interactive terminal UI.
.TP
.B lazydeck serve
Start the local HTTP API used by the Godot and Unity editor integrations.
The server publishes its authenticated connection file at
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lazydeck/serve.json
on Linux.
.TP
.B lazydeck serve --fixture
Start the API using an in-memory backend. This is intended for integration
tests and does not connect to a Steam device.
.TP
.B lazydeck mcp
Run a Model Context Protocol server over stdio. By default it registers only
read-only tools for health, capabilities, configured devices, mDNS discovery,
device status, deployed games, and job status. Claude Desktop and other MCP
clients can use these tools to answer real-world fleet questions without
leaving chat.
.TP
.B lazydeck mcp --fixture
When auto-starting
.B lazydeck serve,
use the in-memory fixture backend instead of real hardware.
.TP
.B lazydeck mcp --allow-mutations
Also register tools that change device or job state: pair, deploy, sync logs,
cancel jobs, and launch/stop requests. Enable this only when you deliberately
want an LLM client to perform mutating devkit operations.
.TP
.B lazydeck version
Print version and build metadata.
.TP
.B lazydeck help
Print command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lazydeck/devices.toml
Configured Steam devkits. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/lazydeck/devices.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lazydeck/config.yml
Optional custom TUI commands. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/lazydeck/config.yml .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lazydeck/serve.json
Authenticated connection information for editor integrations. This file is
created with mode 0600 and exists only for the desktop session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_PYTHON_DIR
Override the bundled Python bridge location.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_UV
Override the uv executable used to run the Python bridge.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_SSH_STRICT
Set to 1 to reject changed Steam-devkit SSH host keys.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_AUTOSTART
Set to 0 to prevent
.B lazydeck mcp
from auto-starting
.B lazydeck serve
when no healthy connection file exists.
.TP
.B LAZYDECK_BIN
Executable that
.B lazydeck mcp
uses when auto-starting
.B lazydeck serve.
Defaults to the running binary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.br
https://github.com/KevinTCoughlin/lazydeck
